@startuml
title MODRISS Operations and Maintenance — Ongoing Kanban Service-Delivery Process
skinparam backgroundColor #F5F3ED
skinparam shadowing false
start
:G7 accepts first live release;
repeat
  :Review SLO, security, product and cost signals;
  :Visualize demand as WP-30 in Requested;
  :Triage, classify and replenish Ready within capacity;
  :Pull into In Progress under WP-31 WIP and SLE policies;
  if (Emergency restoration?) then (yes)
    :Restore under visible expedite policy;
    :Track temporary change until removed or reconciled;
  else (no)
    :Execute selected service or maintenance work;
  endif
  :Verify evidence and update flow measures;
  if (Disposition?) then (operations-only)
    :Close with operational evidence;
  elseif (product change) then (bounded MDE/release)
    :Send to earliest Development and Delivery source;\nreceive released evidence before closure;
  else (future planned release)
    :Commit explicitly to release backlog;
  endif
  :Review flow, quality, cost and process outcomes;
repeat while (Any live release remains?) is (continue pull flow)
:Complete operational shutdown evidence;
:Accept shared G8 closure only when no live release remains;
stop
note right
  Activities and feedback cadences are not phases.
  Board: Requested → Ready → In Progress → Verify → Done.
end note
@enduml
